  "note": "Annual election of one third (five seats) due on Saturday 15 January 1910. Only four councillors retired (Ballentine, Ferguson, Lonsdale and White); the fifth seat had been vacant for almost two years after the death of its holder. Eight were nominated on Wednesday 5 January; on Thursday J. Vernon Malcomson, Joseph Holland and John Houston withdrew, and the four retiring members and T. M. Livingston (new) were returned unopposed. Folder dated the statutory polling day. No party labels printed."
